(GENERAL EDITORS? PREFACE) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The Editors hope to issue in this series of International Medical) Tj T*
(Monographs contributions to the domain of the Medical Sciences on) Tj T*
(subjects of immediate interest, made by first-hand authorities who have) Tj T*
(been engaged in extending the confines of knowledge. Readers who seek) Tj T*
(to follow the rapid progress made in some new phase of investigation) Tj T*
(will find therein accurate information acquired from the consultation) Tj T*
(of the leading authorities of Europe and America, and illuminated by) Tj T*
(the researches and considered opinions of the authors.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Amidst the press and rush of modern research, and the multitude of) Tj T*
(papers published in many tongues, it is necessary to find men of proved) Tj T*
(merit and ripe experience, who will winnow the wheat from the chaff,) Tj T*
(and give us the present knowledge of their own subjects in a duly) Tj T*
(balanced, concise, and accurate form.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This volume deals with a subject of wide interest, for lead is dealt) Tj T*
(with in so many important processes of manufacture--in the making of) Tj T*
(white lead; pottery glazing; glass polishing; handling of printing) Tj T*
(type; litho-making; house, coach, and motor painting; manufacture of) Tj T*
(paints and colour; file-making; tinning of metals; harness-making;) Tj T*
(manufacture of accumulators, etc.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The authors bring forward convincing evidence, experimental and) Tj T*
(statistical, in favour of the causation of lead poisoning by the) Tj T*
(inhalation of dust. This makes prevention a comparatively simple) Tj T*
(matter, and the methods of prevention are effective, and will) Tj T*
(contribute greatly to the health of the workers and the prevention of) Tj T*
(phthisis, which is so prevalent among lead-workers. Exhaust fans and) Tj T*
(hoods, or vacuum cleaners, for carrying away the dust formed in the) Tj T*
(various processes--these are the simple means by which the dust can be) Tj T*
(removed and the workers? health assured.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  LEONARD HILL.) Tj T*
(  WILLIAM BULLOCH.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  _September, 1912._) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(AUTHORS? PREFACE) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Progress in the knowledge of the use of lead, the pathology of lead) Tj T*
(poisoning, and the means of preventing or mitigating the risk from it,) Tj T*
