(The degree of resistance exhibited by any given population towards the) Tj T*
(poisonous influence of lead shows considerable variation. Thus, in a) Tj T*
(community using a water-supply contaminated with lead, only a small) Tj T*
(proportion of the persons drinking the water becomes poisoned. There) Tj T*
(are, of course, other factors than that of individual idiosyncrasy) Tj T*
(which may determine the effect of the poison, as, for example, the) Tj T*
(drawing of the water first thing in the morning which has been standing) Tj T*
(in a particular pipe. But even if all disturbing factors are eliminated) Tj T*
(in water-borne lead poisoning, differing degrees of susceptibility are) Tj T*
(always to be observed among the persons using the water.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Lead does not differ, therefore, from any other drugs to which persons) Tj T*
(show marked idiosyncrasies. Thus, very small doses of arsenic may) Tj T*
