(individuals are highly susceptible to some drugs, such as cannabis) Tj T*
(indica, while others are able to ingest large doses without exhibiting) Tj T*
(any sign of poisoning; and it is well known that even in susceptible) Tj T*
(persons the quantity of a particular drug which first produces symptoms) Tj T*
(of poisoning may be gradually increased, if the dosage be continued) Tj T*
(over long periods in quantities insufficient to produce marked symptoms) Tj T*
(of poisoning. In this direction a number of experiments have been) Tj T*
(performed with arsenic, particularly those of Cloetta[1], who found) Tj T*
(that the dose of arsenic for dogs could be gradually raised, if given) Tj T*
(by the mouth, to many times the ordinary fatal dose, but that if at) Tj T*
(this point a subminimal fatal dose was injected beneath the skin acute) Tj T*
(symptoms of arsenic poisoning followed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
