(=Predisposing Causes of Lead Poisoning.=--In lead poisoning, as in many) Tj T*
(other diseases, a number of predisposing and contributory causes may be) Tj T*
(cited which tend to lower the susceptibility of the individual to the) Tj T*
(poisonous effect of the metal and its compounds, or to so modify the) Tj T*
(functions of the body that a smaller dose of poison may produce more) Tj T*
(profound changes than would otherwise be the case.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Certain diseases may be regarded as predisposing causes by lowering the) Tj T*
(general resistance of the body tissues to the influence of lead, and a) Tj T*
(consideration of the chapter on Pathology will at once demonstrate how) Tj T*
(seriously certain diseases may contribute in this way.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
