(bloodvessels, and it will therefore follow that any disease which may) Tj T*
(affect the intima of the bloodvessels may predispose to lead poisoning;) Tj T*
(and, further, as the elimination of lead takes place to a certain) Tj T*
(extent through the kidney, any disease which affects either the renal) Tj T*
(epithelium or the general maintenance of the excretory function of) Tj T*
(the kidney may predispose that organ to the irritative effects of the) Tj T*
(lead circulating in the blood. In the same way, the condition of lead) Tj T*
(absorption in which the balance of absorption and elimination of lead) Tj T*
(remains in such a ratio that no definite symptoms of lead poisoning) Tj T*
(appear may have that delicate balance easily upset by the introduction) Tj T*
(of some secondary cause, which, when operating in association with lead) Tj T*
(absorption, may precipitate symptoms attributable to poisoning by that) Tj T*
(metal. Chronic alcoholism especially, producing as it does definite) Tj T*
(changes in the kidney of itself--changes which it is impossible to) Tj T*
(distinguish by the naked eye from the effects of lead poisoning--must) Tj T*
(clearly act as a predisposing, if not even an exciting, cause of lead) Tj T*
(kidney infection. In experiments upon animals, it was found that the) Tj T*
(addition of alcohol to the diet of an animal which was the subject of) Tj T*
(chronic lead absorption precipitated the attack of definite poisoning;) Tj T*
(in other words, the latent period of lead poisoning--that is to) Tj T*
(say, the resistance exhibited by the tissues to the toxic influence) Tj T*
(of lead--was considerably diminished by this addition of a second) Tj T*
