() Tj T*
(In addition to the diseases mentioned which may be said to predispose) Tj T*
(to lead poisoning, certain other diseases have been stated to be) Tj T*
(predisposed to by the action of lead. It is no doubt a fact that where) Tj T*
(chronic anæmia, wasting, loss of subcutaneous fat, decreased muscular) Tj T*
(power, and general lowering of the metabolic activity of the body,) Tj T*
(are produced, an individual so affected may be supposed to be more) Tj T*
(susceptible to certain infectious diseases, and among these stress has) Tj T*
(been laid on the alleged association of phthisis with lead absorption.) Tj T*
(This point is discussed in the next chapter.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In summing up the difficult question of predisposition to lead) Tj T*
(poisoning, together with the correlated questions of susceptibility and) Tj T*
(immunity, certain facts may at any rate be clearly stated:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Undoubted individual susceptibility and immunity exist with regard) Tj T*
(to lead poisoning in exactly the same way as individual susceptibility) Tj T*
(and immunity may be shown to exist towards poisoning by many other) Tj T*
(metals and drugs. Therefore, given the same opportunities for) Tj T*
(infection, a person showing early signs of lead absorption may be) Tj T*
(regarded as susceptible.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Females are at least twice, and probably three times, as susceptible) Tj T*
(to lead poisoning as are males. Much of this susceptibility is) Tj T*
(determined by the extra stress thrown upon the female generative organs.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Certain diseases predispose to lead poisoning mainly by nature of) Tj T*
(the alterations in metabolism produced--chiefly anæmia.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Many persons engaged in lead industries become gradually tolerant of) Tj T*
(the absorption of lead, and in time resist much larger doses than would) Tj T*
(have been possible at the commencement of exposure, but in such persons) Tj T*
(the balance between absorption and excretion upon which that tolerance) Tj T*
(depends may become easily disturbed by intercurrent disease or sudden) Tj T*
(increase in absorption.) Tj T*
