(other industries, and other industries\), the chronic nature of the) Tj T*
(plumbism is markedly above the average, and some severe symptom,) Tj T*
(usually paralysis, is also above the average. An exception to this) Tj T*
(rule is china and earthenware, where severity is considerably below) Tj T*
(the average, but where, among men, the figures for chronic lead) Tj T*
(poisoning and paralysis are distinctly high. It will be seen, however,) Tj T*
(that the proportion of slight cases even in this industry is below) Tj T*
(the average. On the other hand, severity is below the average in) Tj T*
(smelting, white lead, red lead, litho-transfers, enamelling, electric) Tj T*
(accumulators, paints and colours, and coach-painting, and the symptoms) Tj T*
(in these industries are, in general, colic rather than high degree of) Tj T*
(paralysis; but in them a severe symptom which is above the average,) Tj T*
(in general, is encephalopathy. The explanation of these differences) Tj T*
(depends, we believe, on two factors: \(1\) Duration of employment, with) Tj T*
(which, naturally, the age of the worker is associated; \(2\) opportunity) Tj T*
(of inhaling lead dust. The longer the employment, the more likely,) Tj T*
(naturally, if absorption goes on, is the plumbism to become chronic,) Tj T*
(and to be associated with paralysis, its prominent sign. Duration of) Tj T*
(employment among males in file-cutting and china and earthenware, as) Tj T*
(contrasted, for instance, with that in white lead, is very much longer,) Tj T*
(and the same could be shown of comparatively new industries, such as) Tj T*
(electric accumulators and litho-transfers. Thus, in one year the age) Tj T*
