(Persons employed in the manufacture of white and red lead, electric) Tj T*
(accumulators, paints and colours, and the others named, are exposed) Tj T*
(essentially to dust from salts of lead, which are readily absorbed.) Tj T*
(Poisoning, therefore, if precautions are inadequate, will quickly show) Tj T*
(itself, causing certain workers to seek other employment after one) Tj T*
(attack. Poisoning thus produced is more likely to induce colic, or,) Tj T*
(if the dose has been large or the individual markedly susceptible,) Tj T*
(encephalopathic symptoms, than paralysis. On the other hand, the) Tj T*
(slowness of the onset of symptoms in the case of brass workers,) Tj T*
(plumbers, printers, file-cutters, and tinners, is more the result) Tj T*
(of inhalation of fumes or of dust of metallic lead than of salts of) Tj T*
(lead; or if the inhalation be of salts of lead, then of these in less) Tj T*
(amount and over a long period, with, as a result, gradual undermining) Tj T*
(of the constitution, showing itself in paralysis, arterio-sclerosis,) Tj T*
