(Other conditions which might readily be admitted as sequelæ are) Tj T*
(optic neuritis, following on an attack of encephalopathy. No general) Tj T*
(statement can be made in regard to mental and nervous diseases, gout,) Tj T*
(pernicious anæmia, as sequelæ, as each must be considered in relation) Tj T*
(to the evidence adduced in the particular case, and after exclusion, in) Tj T*
(the first two, of syphilis as a cause.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The distinction between causation and association has to be borne) Tj T*
(in mind before admitting as sequelæ of lead poisoning diseases of) Tj T*
(bacterial origin, such as phthisis or pneumonia, or any disease to) Tj T*
(which the affected person may be thought to have been rendered more) Tj T*
(prone by reason of lead employment. The contention that a person) Tj T*
(may have been debilitated by lead poisoning is no proof that the) Tj T*
(enfeeblement of the constitution was the cause either of the bacillus) Tj T*
(gaining entrance into the lung or of the ultimate fatal issue from) Tj T*
(the engrafted disease. Such assertion in every case must rest on) Tj T*
(supposition. Evidence that lead employment predisposes to phthisis is) Tj T*
(not necessarily made stronger, in our opinion, by existence during) Tj T*
(life of clinical symptoms, or, in their absence, of detection of lead) Tj T*
(in the tissues post mortem.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In classifying causes of death, the general rule should be to select,) Tj T*
(from the several diseases mentioned in the certificate, the disease) Tj T*
(of the longest duration. Exceptions to this rule are that definite) Tj T*
(diseases ordinarily known as constitutional diseases should have) Tj T*
(preference over the other diseases mentioned. After thirty-five years) Tj T*
(of age, certificates of death from lead poisoning are almost always) Tj T*
(filled in in association with other diseases which are the usual causes) Tj T*
(which lead to mortality generally. But neither phthisis, nor pneumonia,) Tj T*
(nor any acute disease of the heart or lungs, nor valvular disease of) Tj T*
(the heart, nor, indeed, any acute febrile condition, can have direct) Tj T*
(relation with--_i.e._, be a sequela of--lead poisoning.) Tj T*
