(  A very complete histological examination was made of the brain and) Tj T*
(  spinal cord, and throughout the particular changes noticed were) Tj T*
(  proliferation of the glia, hyaline thickening of the walls of the) Tj T*
(  vessels, both arteries and veins, and presence of congestion; and) Tj T*
(  here and there rupture of the smallest vessels, causing miliary) Tj T*
(  microscopic hæmorrhages into the perivascular sheaths and the) Tj T*
(  substance of the brain. There was no infiltration with lymphocytes) Tj T*
(  and plasma cells, as is found in general paralysis. The neuroglia) Tj T*
(  showed a formative hyperplasia resulting from chronic irritation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  In the cortex there was neuroglia proliferation in the polymorpho) Tj T*
(  layer and the molecular layer. Changes were seen in the Betz cells,) Tj T*
(  particularly in the Nissl substance, with perinuclear chromatolysis,) Tj T*
(  such as is generally found in chronic peripheral neuritis, whether) Tj T*
(  due to lead, alcohol, or other toxic causes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  There was no coarse atrophy or degeneration of the fibres of the) Tj T*
(  cortex. Neither the cerebellum nor the spinal cord at any of the) Tj T*
(  levels examined showed fibre atrophy or degeneration, except possibly) Tj T*
(  a slight diffuse sclerosis in the crossed pyramidal tracts of the) Tj T*
(  lumbar region.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  Microscopical examination was made of the heart, spleen, kidney,) Tj T*
(  liver, lung, and suprarenal gland. There was a general condition) Tj T*
(  of angiosclerosis; in the liver a fibrotic overgrowth around the) Tj T*
(  vessels; in the kidneys well-marked interstitial fibrosis.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  A chemical examination of the brain was also conducted by the copper) Tj T*
(  potassium nitrite method, but no lead was found.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=Excretory System.=--A large number of observers have shown that great) Tj T*
(stress is thrown on the kidney in the excretion of lead. Discussion) Tj T*
(has taken place as to whether the effect is a primary interstitial) Tj T*
(or a parenchymatous nephritis. Most observers are agreed that the) Tj T*
(histological changes found in the kidneys of lead workers have very) Tj T*
(little by which they may be differentiated from the effects of alcohol.) Tj T*
