(resist destruction when making films, than in normal blood.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There is thus very striking continuity in the observations of all) Tj T*
(the various observers, despite the fact that at first sight their) Tj T*
(descriptions may appear discordant. There seems no doubt that) Tj T*
(practically all authors who have given attention to the subject are) Tj T*
(agreed that the circulatory system, and primarily the blood circulating) Tj T*
(in the vessels, is affected by lead, and, further, that the vessels) Tj T*
