(the food would tend to prevent the lead having a toxic or deleterious) Tj T*
(effect, but even when the lead was given in the form of pills between) Tj T*
(meals no poisonous effect was noticed. Further, the quantity of white) Tj T*
(lead given was considerable, and it is highly questionable whether) Tj T*
(the quantity of lead so taken would be dissolved by the gastric) Tj T*
(juice excreted under normal circumstances in its entirety, as a) Tj T*
(very considerable quantity would pass onwards through the pylorus) Tj T*
