() Tj T*
(The increased susceptibility to lead poisoning through the agency of) Tj T*
(alcohol is interesting. No. 6 received, in addition to its inhalations) Tj T*
(or period of exposure in the dusty air, 50 c.c. of port wine per diem.) Tj T*
(Symptoms of lead poisoning appeared a day sooner than in any other) Tj T*
(animal, and if we eliminate this experiment, as the dust \(flue dust) Tj T*
(from blast-furnace\) contained also arsenic and antimony, three days) Tj T*
(sooner than the litharge animal, and twenty-five days sooner than the) Tj T*
(other animals exposed to white lead dust. In addition, this animal was) Tj T*
(the only one which actually died during the period of experiment; all) Tj T*
(the other animals were killed at the end of two months and submitted) Tj T*
(to histological examination; but the animal which had received alcohol) Tj T*
(died with symptoms closely simulating lead encephalopathy in man. The) Tj T*
(predisposing action of alcohol is still further emphasized by the) Tj T*
(subsequent experiments with three animals exposed to white lead dust;) Tj T*
