() Tj T*
(In the case of animals fed with white lead, one after eight months,) Tj T*
(and the other a year and a half, showed no signs of lead poisoning) Tj T*
(at all, while the weights remained constant. At the end of this time) Tj T*
(alcohol \(50 c.c. of port wine\) was added to the animals? diet, and one) Tj T*
(month after the addition of alcohol to the diet, the dose of white) Tj T*
(lead being continued constant, encephalopathy ensued. In a second case) Tj T*
(the animal was started on alcohol in addition to the white lead. In a) Tj T*
(month it was showing signs of slight paresis. Again, an animal fed on) Tj T*
(a low-solubility frit consisting of ground-up lead silicate, showed) Tj T*
