(end of this time alcohol was added to its diet, and six months later) Tj T*
(the animal developed symptoms of cerebral involvement, which continued) Tj T*
(at intervals until a fatal attack of encephalopathy at the end of a) Tj T*
(year. There is thus definite evidence to show that the addition of) Tj T*
(alcohol to the animal?s diet undoubtedly hastened and determined the) Tj T*
(appearance of lead poisoning, and this, taken in conjunction with the) Tj T*
(inhalation experiments previously cited, is very strong evidence of the) Tj T*
(increased susceptibility to lead poisoning produced by alcohol. This) Tj T*
(supersensitiveness to lead through the medium of alcohol is a matter) Tj T*
(of clinical experience to most persons who have had experience of) Tj T*
(industrial lead poisoning, particularly those who have been engaged in) Tj T*
(the routine examination of persons working in factories.) Tj T*
