(=Inoculation Experiments.=--In order to control both the feeding and) Tj T*
(the inhalation experiments, and more particularly to obtain direct) Tj T*
(information of the effect of lead upon the body tissues, resource was) Tj T*
(had to the inoculation of the various lead compounds tested--namely:) Tj T*
(\(1\) White lead, \(2\) litharge, \(3\) lead frit. These three compounds are) Tj T*
(the three types of lead salt which are used in the Potteries, whilst) Tj T*
(white lead and litharge are the compounds causing industrial poisoning) Tj T*
(in the largest proportion of cases in other industries. As a further) Tj T*
(control, the more soluble lead salts were also made use of--namely,) Tj T*
(acetate, nitrate, and chloride--mainly for the purpose of establishing) Tj T*
(some standard of poisoning both in rate and dose.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Several rather unexpected results were derived from the inoculation) Tj T*
(experiments, which will be referred to.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The method of inoculation was to suspend the lead compound to be) Tj T*
(tested in normal saline solution or distilled water. The animal was) Tj T*
(then shaved, and the lead compound inoculated into the muscles of the) Tj T*
(back. The corrosive action of these lead salts was avoided by using a) Tj T*
(considerable quantity of diluent.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Lead frit is a constituent of low-solubility glaze--that is to say, a) Tj T*
(glaze which has not more than 5 per cent. soluble lead when subjected) Tj T*
(to the standard test of exposing 1 gramme of the glaze to a litre of) Tj T*
(0·04 per cent. hydrochloric acid for an hour at room temperature. The) Tj T*
(frit which was the constituent of this glaze is produced by heating) Tj T*
(together litharge or lead and silica, the production being a yellow,) Tj T*
(hard, glaze-like material looking very much like sugar-candy. It is not) Tj T*
(by any means a compound of lead and silica of simple composition, as) Tj T*
(different samples show a wide variation in their lead content; whilst,) Tj T*
(in addition, the mode of its formation closely resembles that of an) Tj T*
(alloy or amalgam, and allows of the formation of a eutectic entangling) Tj T*
(in its meshes both of the constituents of which it is formed, so) Tj T*
(that a certain amount of free lead, in addition to the silicates of) Tj T*
(various descriptions, are present. At the same time the compound is) Tj T*
(highly resistant to the action of mineral acids, and, of course, much) Tj T*
(more insoluble and refractory than white lead, litharge, or other) Tj T*
(lead oxides. The body fluids, however, particularly the fluids in the) Tj T*
(subcutaneous and muscular tissue, definitely exert some action upon) Tj T*
(this fritted lead, and it was found experimentally that symptoms of) Tj T*
(poisoning could be produced in the experimental animals when even small) Tj T*
(doses were administered. A gramme of frit was inoculated, and in all) Tj T*
(but one case the animals showed definite signs of lead poisoning, and) Tj T*
(in two instances actually died with symptoms of encephalitis.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
