() Tj T*
(The experiments definitely bring out one all-important fact--namely,) Tj T*
(that lead dust circulating in the air is many times more dangerous than) Tj T*
(lead actually swallowed; for even if the animals which were exposed to) Tj T*
(the inhalation of dust swallowed the whole of the quantity contained) Tj T*
(in the respired air, they would only obtain one-tenth of the amount) Tj T*
(the other fed animals were getting. It is, of course, impossible to) Tj T*
(suppose that the whole of the lead contained in the inhaled air reached) Tj T*
(the lung. It can only have been the smaller particles which did so.) Tj T*
(Therefore the ratio is many more than ten times between the fed and the) Tj T*
