(the lumbar region\), out of proportion to the determined loss of weight;) Tj T*
(pinched facies, with frequent exhibition of running from the eyes and) Tj T*
(nose, even when not exposed to the action of lead dust, merely by) Tj T*
(inoculation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Various types of paralysis, particularly in the cat; the muscles of) Tj T*
(the back and of the quadriceps extensor of the hind-legs show signs of) Tj T*
(paralysis. In the cat the quadriceps extensor is paralyzed sooner than) Tj T*
(the extensor communis digitorum in man. The cats show loss of power in) Tj T*
(the hind-limbs by inability to jump. The reflexes, particularly the) Tj T*
(knee-jerks and elbow-jerks, are first of all increased, and latterly) Tj T*
(become lost.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The chief and main sign which was noted in the histological examination) Tj T*
(of the animals inoculated was one of minute microscopical hæmorrhages) Tj T*
(\(this has already been referred to\); these hæmorrhages were not) Tj T*
(confined to any particular position in the body nor to any one organ.) Tj T*
(In the animals which showed symptoms of epilepsy, occasionally) Tj T*
(thickening of the pia mater was found, but invariably in such cases) Tj T*
(small hæmorrhages were found immediately under the arachnoid, not) Tj T*
(covering any great area, but apparently causing pressure upon small) Tj T*
(areas of the cortex. In others, again, the hæmorrhages were found) Tj T*
(lower down in the brain, and a few in the spinal cord. At times a) Tj T*
(large amount of hæmorrhage was to be found present at the base of the) Tj T*
