(Finally, in summing up the conclusions to be drawn from the above) Tj T*
(experiments, it has been suggested that such experiments as) Tj T*
(inoculation, experimental inhalation, or even feeding, are no criterion) Tj T*
(of the circumstances under which industrial workers become infected) Tj T*
(with lead. It is perhaps hardly necessary to refer to this point, but) Tj T*
(for the fact that it is possible this book may be made use of by those) Tj T*
(who are not in the habit of dealing with experimental pathology. One) Tj T*
(of the first and most important matters in dealing with any form of) Tj T*
(poisoning is to obtain knowledge of the actual symptoms both clinically) Tj T*
(and physiologically, as well as pathologically, of the effects of any) Tj T*
(drug, and to determine if the symptoms so produced in an experimental) Tj T*
(animal conform to the symptoms as seen in man. For the purpose,) Tj T*
(therefore, an animal is required which is susceptible to the poison,) Tj T*
(and therefore cats were used in the foregoing experiments, as it is) Tj T*
(absolutely impossible to keep a domesticated cat in any white lead) Tj T*
(works, for the animals invariably become poisoned by lead.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The second point in prosecuting an inquiry into the pathology of any) Tj T*
(disease is to determine the train of poisoning when definite dosage,) Tj T*
(both in quantity and compound, is made use of. By feeding an animal) Tj T*
(with a compound only, the absorption through the gastro-intestinal) Tj T*
(canal could be studied; whereas by inoculating some of the compound--in) Tj T*
(suspension if it be insoluble, or in solution if it be soluble--into) Tj T*
(the subcutaneous or muscular tissue, the direct action of the) Tj T*
(body fluids on the compound may be studied; and, furthermore, its) Tj T*
(absorption by the membranes--that is, the cell membranes and the animal) Tj T*
(tissues--are determined. It is necessary to give at first a dose big) Tj T*
(enough to produce definite symptoms, and then to gradually decrease the) Tj T*
(dose to find the minimum amount producing symptoms within a reasonable) Tj T*
(amount of time. Inoculation experiments therefore give an answer to a) Tj T*
(number of these questions, and are the basis upon which further inquiry) Tj T*
(is conducted; they form a criterion from which it is possible to judge) Tj T*
(the effect of inhalation, and the same remarks which have been made) Tj T*
(with regard to inoculation refer to inhalation experiments. It is) Tj T*
(essential first of all, in the experimental animals, to subject them) Tj T*
(to rigorous enough conditions to obtain definite symptoms, and then,) Tj T*
(by varying the experiments, to study the amount, entrance, and general) Tj T*
(behaviour, of the poison, correlating the evidence so obtained from the) Tj T*
(definite knowledge already gained with the previous experiments.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(It is hoped that this brief note on experimental evidence will assist) Tj T*
(in the elucidation of the foregoing experiments to those who are not) Tj T*
(conversant with the application of experimental evidence.) Tj T*
