(=The Anæmia of Lead Poisoning and Saturnine Anæmia.=--From the early) Tj T*
(days of medicine it has been known that lead produces poverty of the) Tj T*
(blood, and the white or yellowish-white appearance of persons who have) Tj T*
(been subjected to long-continued inhalation of lead dust or fumes) Tj T*
(constitutes striking evidence of blood-alteration. At the same time) Tj T*
(it is a common fact that the facial pallor does not always go hand in) Tj T*
(hand with diminution in the hæmoglobin. The conjunctiva may be observed) Tj T*
(as a test for colour, and here may be seen the curious vaso-motor) Tj T*
(disturbances which are partially responsible for the facial pallor.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Facial pallor in some forms of lead cachexia owes its origin to) Tj T*
(interference with the nerve-supply to the vessel walls, and it is) Tj T*
(a noticeable fact that a lead-worker whose face shows unmistakable) Tj T*
(signs of pallor rapidly flushes when spoken to suddenly or if mentally) Tj T*
(disturbed. The anæmia of lead poisoning is, however, a very definite) Tj T*
(fact. All observers are agreed that a marked diminution in the) Tj T*
(hæmoglobin of the blood takes place, to as low, often, as 35 per cent.,) Tj T*
(without necessitating abstention from work, and without any serious) Tj T*
(interference with respiration, even when performing heavy manual labour.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In persons in whom the hæmoglobin is diminished there is frequently a) Tj T*
(yellowish or icterous hue of the skin, particularly the conjunctiva,) Tj T*
(due to staining of the tissues with altered blood-pigment. The) Tj T*
(hæmoglobin derivative--hæmatoporphyrin--can also be found in the) Tj T*
(urine of persons suffering from a marked degree of reduction in the) Tj T*
(blood-pigment, and may be taken as confirmatory evidence of destructive) Tj T*
(or hæmolytic anæmia. The symptom is, however, a later one than is) Tj T*
(frequently stated by the French observers, and can only be regarded as) Tj T*
(a later and confirmatory symptom, and not as an early one of diagnostic) Tj T*
(importance.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(As would be expected from the destruction of blood-pigment, the) Tj T*
(morbid process leaves its imprint upon the individual red cells, and) Tj T*
(basophile staining of a number of the red corpuscles is to be found in) Tj T*
(a very large proportion of persons poisoned by lead. Moritz[6] first) Tj T*
