(blood-cells in addition to the basophile staining. Distinct vacuoles) Tj T*
(appear, but as a general observation--first noted by Glibert[8]--the) Tj T*
(blood appears to be more resistant to damage when making the films,) Tj T*
(and the red corpuscles themselves seem to be more elastic than normal) Tj T*
