(of paralysis; for if we accept the view that lead is a poison that) Tj T*
(has a selective power on certain nerves, we have still to consider) Tj T*
(which is the greatest force, the selection of certain groups of) Tj T*
(muscles or the effect of functional action. The theory of muscular) Tj T*
(overexertion certainly falls in with the type of paralysis, and Teleky) Tj T*
(has undoubtedly shown that under certain circumstances, by special) Tj T*
(exertion of other muscle groups not usually affected, these muscles) Tj T*
(alone, or to a greater extent than those usually affected, are involved) Tj T*
(in the paresis. If, therefore, lead has a selective action, which is) Tj T*
(exceedingly doubtful, it must be very slight.) Tj T*
