(acid, after repeated incinerations, finally extracting with ammonium) Tj T*
(acetate. Filter, incinerate, and take up the residue in dilute nitric) Tj T*
(acid. Evaporate to dryness and add a few drops of dilute acetic acid,) Tj T*
(and transfer drop to microscope slide.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To the drop on the microscope slide add one drop of dilute copper) Tj T*
(acetate solution, and two to three drops of saturated solution of) Tj T*
(potassium nitrate. Stir up the drops and well mix with a platinum wire,) Tj T*
(allow to stand for a few minutes, and then examine with a two-thirds) Tj T*
(objective. If lead is present, violet-black cubes of potassium copper) Tj T*
(lead nitrate appear \(K?CuPb[NO?]\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This test is said to give a reaction in the presence of 0·00003 gramme.) Tj T*
