() Tj T*
(2. =Quantitative Methods of Estimation.=--Two methods may be used in) Tj T*
(the detection of lead in organic substances, either in organic fluids) Tj T*
(or in solids, and are generally termed the ?wet? and ?dry? methods,) Tj T*
(from the original treatment of the substance.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the dry method the substance is incinerated with or without the) Tj T*
(addition of sulphuric and nitric acid; in the wet the material is) Tj T*
(treated with hydrochloric acid and potassium chlorate. Subsequent) Tj T*
(treatment in both cases is on the same lines.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Method of Fresenius and Von Babo[5]--Moist Method._--The substance) Tj T*
(which is suspected to contain the poison, if solid, is reduced to a) Tj T*
(pulp, and is mixed with sufficient water until of the consistency of) Tj T*
(thin gruel. The urine should be evaporated to one-fourth or one-sixth) Tj T*
(of its volume. Fæces should be well stirred up with distilled water.) Tj T*
(The substance is then placed in a large flask together with crystals) Tj T*
(of potassium chlorate; each 100 grammes of the substance require 3 to) Tj T*
(4 grammes of potassium chlorate. Pure HCl of the same weight as the) Tj T*
(original substance is then added, the flask is placed on a water-bath) Tj T*
(and gently heated. Care must be taken that the heating is not too) Tj T*
(brisk, as otherwise the evolution of the chlorine peroxide takes place) Tj T*
(too rapidly. If necessary, additional crystals of potassium chlorate) Tj T*
(are added from time to time until the fluid becomes limpid and of a) Tj T*
(slight yellow colour, or, if there is much organic matter, until it) Tj T*
(assumes the appearance and colour of thin oatmeal gruel. On account of) Tj T*
(more gradual evolution of chlorine, the chlorate that is present before) Tj T*
(the flask is heated acts much more energetically, weight for weight,) Tj T*
(than fragments added after the liquid is heated, as a great deal of) Tj T*
(the gas then escapes without rendering any service. If the substance) Tj T*
(contains sugar, starch, or alcohol, extra care must be taken to avoid) Tj T*
(frothing over. When the fluid contents are clear or reduced to a thin) Tj T*
(consistency, the liquid is transferred to an evaporating basin, and) Tj T*
(allowed to remain on a water-bath until the smell of chlorine has) Tj T*
(disappeared; it is then filtered while hot. The whole of the organic) Tj T*
