(of vegetable parchment, the outer cell containing distilled water) Tj T*
(acidulated with H?SO?. Into the inner cell is placed a piece of) Tj T*
(platinum-foil measuring about 50 square centimetres of exposed) Tj T*
(surface, which is connected with the kathode or negative pole of four) Tj T*
(Grove cells, and into the outer cell is placed a like-sized piece) Tj T*
(of platinum-foil connected with the anode or positive pole. These) Tj T*
(pieces of foil are so placed in relation to one another that they) Tj T*
(are only separated by the parchment. The galvanic circuit being now) Tj T*
(closed for some hours, any lead in the filtrate will be deposited) Tj T*
(on the platinum-foil connected with the kathode in the inner cell.) Tj T*
