(In laying down the general lines of treatment for both lead poisoning) Tj T*
(and lead absorption, it is essential in the first place to distinguish) Tj T*
(carefully between the two states; for although lead absorption may) Tj T*
(gradually drift into definite lead intoxication and lead poisoning,) Tj T*
(with all the classical symptoms associated with the saturnine cachexia,) Tj T*
(a large number of cases, particularly those in industrial processes,) Tj T*
(do not and should not progress beyond the early symptoms of lead) Tj T*
(absorption. The treatment, therefore, will depend in the first place on) Tj T*
(whether the case be one so constantly met with in industrial processes,) Tj T*
(where generalized symptoms of lead absorption are manifest without any) Tj T*
(definite and disabling symptoms traceable and sufficiently pronounced) Tj T*
(to enable a diagnosis of lead poisoning to be made.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The facts given in the chapter on Pathology, on the methods of entrance) Tj T*
(of lead, on the toxic manifestations, and the blood-changes, and, above) Tj T*
(all, the facts relating to microscopical hæmorrhages and other profound) Tj T*
(changes in the bloodvessels, point clearly to the lines along which the) Tj T*
(general treatment for amelioration, prevention, or cure of poisoning) Tj T*
(should be undertaken.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The treatment of the so-called ?presaturnine state,? or what is) Tj T*
(preferably termed the ?state of lead absorption,? is one that the) Tj T*
(appointed surgeon or certifying surgeon in lead factories or other) Tj T*
(processes in which lead is manufactured or used, is constantly called) Tj T*
(upon to treat. Lead poisoning is a definite entity as a disabling) Tj T*
(disease, whereas lead absorption, although the prodromal stage of) Tj T*
(such disease, cannot be defined as actual lead poisoning, as in many) Tj T*
(instances persons may show signs of continued lead absorption, but) Tj T*
(their powers of elimination can be maintained at such a level that the) Tj T*
(ratio of absorption to elimination remains in equilibrium.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(With the preventive treatment of lead poisoning we have dealt in) Tj T*
(another place \(see p. 199\). What is particularly required here is the) Tj T*
(medicinal treatment, which may be helpful in preventing lead absorption) Tj T*
(passing on to definite lead poisoning.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For many years it has been customary in the treatment of men employed) Tj T*
(in lead works to give occasional purgatives, and it is, moreover, a) Tj T*
(common and proper precaution to keep a stock of some simple aperient) Tj T*
(medicine, preferably saline composed of sodium sulphate and magnesium) Tj T*
(sulphate, at the works in charge of the foreman, so that any man who) Tj T*
(so desires may obtain a dose of an ordinary aperient mixture. We) Tj T*
(have seen from the pathological evidence that the largest proportion) Tj T*
(of lead is excreted by the bowel, and that, therefore, the sweeping) Tj T*
(away of the bowel contents--particularly where constipation is set) Tj T*
(up--will naturally tend to remove from the body a good deal of the) Tj T*
(lead which has been already excreted into the intestine and which) Tj T*
(may presumably become reabsorbed unless it be swept away. In a large) Tj T*
(electric accumulator factory Epsom salts in the form of the granular) Tj T*
(effervescing preparation is much appreciated. In winter 50 per cent.,) Tj T*
