(opinion amongst various physicians as to the efficacy of the drug in) Tj T*
(the elimination of lead from the body. At the same time a very large) Tj T*
(number of persons hold that the administration of fairly large doses of) Tj T*
(potassium iodide in the case of a person suffering from chronic lead) Tj T*
(absorption may at times be associated with sudden exacerbation of the) Tj T*
(disease, and that the drug apparently may determine the production of) Tj T*
(acute symptoms, such as encephalopathy or paralysis, when these have) Tj T*
(not been previous features of the case. Our experience supports this) Tj T*
(statement, and on more than one occasion one of us \(K. W. G.\) has seen) Tj T*
(a distinct increase of symptoms follow the administration of large) Tj T*
