(be preceded by a long stage of chronic headache with slight or total) Tj T*
(remissions. Headaches may last for several months before the actual) Tj T*
(acute stage of the disease is reached. In the examination of several) Tj T*
(brains of persons who have died from lead encephalitis, microscopic) Tj T*
(sections of the brain have shown signs of hæmorrhages which must have) Tj T*
(taken place some considerable time prior to death, and were no doubt) Tj T*
(associated with the headache that had been complained of for some) Tj T*
(time previously, before the onset of the fatal illness. \(See Plate) Tj T*
(III.\) Persistent headache occurring in a lead-worker should always be) Tj T*
(regarded with grave suspicion, and such a case should be treated on the) Tj T*
(assumption that it is an early case of lead encephalitis. Bromides and) Tj T*
(iodides should be given, and the patient placed in quiet surroundings,) Tj T*
