(In the acute attacks vaso-motor spasm is no doubt partially accountable) Tj T*
(for the symptoms, and various dilators, previously noted in discussing) Tj T*
(colic, may be made use of, such, for instance, as amyl nitrite,) Tj T*
(scopolamine, etc., whilst pyramidon, antipyrin, phenacetin, and other) Tj T*
(similar drugs may be given between the attacks. Under no circumstances) Tj T*
(should any person who has suffered from encephalitis or other cerebral) Tj T*
(symptom of lead poisoning be allowed to resume work in a lead industry.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The treatment of eye affections in lead poisoning requires little) Tj T*
(comment, as the essential treatment must be the same as in other cases,) Tj T*
(mainly devoted towards the elimination of the poison. Attempts may be) Tj T*
(made to treat paresis of the ocular muscles by means of mild electric) Tj T*
(currents, but of this we have had no experience. About 50 per cent. of) Tj T*
(cases of lead amaurosis and amblyopia recover, but a number progress to) Tj T*
(total and permanent blindness, and prognosis in such cases must always) Tj T*
(be guarded.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=Prognosis.=--The prognosis of the first attacks of lead poisoning of) Tj T*
(simple colic or even slight unilateral paresis is good; practically all) Tj T*
(cases recover under proper treatment. It is unusual for a person to) Tj T*
(succumb to a first attack of simple colic, or paresis.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In most cases the serious forms of poisoning only make their appearance) Tj T*
(after three or four previous attacks of colic, but a single attack of) Tj T*
(paresis is much more frequently followed by a severe form of poisoning,) Tj T*
(such as encephalitis.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A limited number of persons are highly susceptible to lead poisoning,) Tj T*
(and these persons rapidly show their susceptibility when working in) Tj T*
(a dangerous lead process. Lead poisoning occurring in an alcoholic) Tj T*
(subject is more likely to result in paretic and mental symptoms than) Tj T*
(in a person who is not addicted to alcohol, and the prognosis of lead) Tj T*
(poisoning in an alcoholic is much less favourable than in the case of a) Tj T*
(normal person.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Mental symptoms very rarely follow from a single attack of lead colic,) Tj T*
(and as a rule do not become established under three or four attacks at) Tj T*
(least.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A small number of persons exposed to excessive doses of lead absorption) Tj T*
(through the lungs develop mental symptoms, such as acute encephalitis,) Tj T*
(without any prodromal stage. The prognosis in such cases is always) Tj T*
(exceedingly grave.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Sudden generalized forms of paralysis are not common in the early) Tj T*
(stages, but are invariably of grave import. A few cases of paresis,) Tj T*
(particularly those of the peroneal type, and affecting the lower limbs,) Tj T*
(become progressive, and eventually develop into a condition resembling) Tj T*
