(The prognosis of simple colic in women is about as good as for males,) Tj T*
(but if an attack of abortion is associated with lead poisoning,) Tj T*
(eclampsia often supervenes and permanent mental derangement may follow.) Tj T*
(In the dementia associated with lead poisoning the prognosis is not) Tj T*
(so grave as in other forms of dementia, especially alcoholic, but) Tj T*
(depression is an unfavourable symptom. The mania of lead poisoning is) Tj T*
(not so noisy as that of alcoholic mania, but where there is suspicion) Tj T*
(of alcoholic as well as lead poisoning the prognosis is exceedingly) Tj T*
(grave.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(As a rule the prognosis of cases of lead poisoning occurring in) Tj T*
(industrial conditions is more favourable when colic is a marked feature) Tj T*
(than when it is absent, and there is no doubt that the prognosis) Tj T*
(in cases of industrial lead poisoning at the present time is more) Tj T*
(favourable than it was before the introduction of exhaust ventilation) Tj T*
(and general medical supervision--a fact no doubt to be explained by the) Tj T*
(relative decrease in the amount of lead absorbed.) Tj T*
