(height of 4 feet from the ground, was found to contain 15·6 per cent.) Tj T*
(of metallic lead. Similarly, a sample taken above a bath for tempering) Tj T*
(railway springs contained 48·1 per cent. metallic lead[1]. And,) Tj T*
(again, a sample collected from the top of the magazine of a linotype) Tj T*
(machine contained 8·18 per cent. Such analyses point to the necessity) Tj T*
(of enclosing, as far as possible, the sources of danger--either the) Tj T*
(fume or the dust, or both. Determination of the melting-point of the) Tj T*
(molten mass will often help in deciding whether there is risk of fume) Tj T*
