(_Exhaust by Fans._--The draught for removal of dust, and frequently) Tj T*
(also of fumes, is produced by a fan, of which there are two types:) Tj T*
(\(1\) low-pressure volume fans and \(2\) high-pressure centrifugal fans.) Tj T*
(In the first the draught is created by the rotation of a wheel with) Tj T*
(inclined vanes, causing the air to be driven transversely through the) Tj T*
(wheel parallel to the axis of rotation \(Fig. 1\). During a revolution) Tj T*
(a portion of the air is cut off from one side of the wheel, and) Tj T*
(transferred through the wheel to the other. Such fans are light, run) Tj T*
(easily, and are cheap. They are of many forms, both with regard to the) Tj T*
(number of blades--from two to eight--and general manner in which they) Tj T*
(are arranged. Some closely resemble the screw-propeller of a ship,) Tj T*
(while others have blades turned over and fastened on an outer rim.) Tj T*
(Their main defect is inability to overcome any but slight resistance) Tj T*
(in the course of suction behind, as from constriction in, or friction) Tj T*
(along the sides of, the ducts and right-angled bends, or of outflow in) Tj T*
(front, as from wind-pressure. Under favourable conditions, however, and) Tj T*
(when carefully fitted, a volume fan will exhaust dust and fumes through) Tj T*
(a system of ducts several feet in length, as, for example, from mono) Tj T*
(and linotype machines and electro melting-pots in letterpress printing) Tj T*
(works. But, in order to avoid resistance from friction, the ducts have) Tj T*
(to be somewhat larger in diameter than when a centrifugal fan is used.) Tj T*
(With nine[A] linotype machines connected up to a 14-inch propeller) Tj T*
(fan, the branch ducts should be about 4 inches in diameter, and the) Tj T*
(main duct 12 inches, increasing from 12 to 15 inches within 2 feet of) Tj T*
(the fan-box. The shorter and straighter the course of the duct to the) Tj T*
(propeller fan, the more efficiently it works. Wind-guards are necessary) Tj T*
(to overcome resistance from this source in front, but their position) Tj T*
(requires to be carefully considered, so as to prevent the screen itself) Tj T*
(crippling the outflow.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  [A] If gratings are also inserted in the same duct for general) Tj T*
(  ventilation the number of machines must be decreased _pro ratâ_.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(All fans require frequent cleaning, and in this respect propeller fans) Tj T*
(have the advantage over centrifugal, in that they are usually more) Tj T*
(accessible.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Illustration: FIG. 2.--DAVIDSON?S DUST CENTRIFUGAL FAN.]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
