() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(_Ducts._--The main duct should be of metal \(steel, sheet-iron, or) Tj T*
(zinc\); it should be circular in shape, have as straight and short a) Tj T*
(course as possible, and be tapered in such manner that the area of) Tj T*
(cross-section at any point shall equal the combined areas of all the) Tj T*
(branch pipes which have entered it at that point \(Fig. 3\). Proper) Tj T*
(dimensions must be studied in relation to the size of the fan and the) Tj T*
(work to be done. Wooden ducts, unless chosen for specific reasons,) Tj T*
(such as the presence of acid in the fumes to be removed, are very) Tj T*
(unsatisfactory, as it is difficult to maintain them in an air-tight) Tj T*
(condition or to make branch pipes enter with rounded junctions. Where) Tj T*
(several branch ducts enter a main duct, situation of the fan midway) Tj T*
(between them has advantage, not only in saving metal in piping, but) Tj T*
(also in causing the distance of the fan from the farthest branch) Tj T*
(duct to be only half what it would be were the fan placed at the end) Tj T*
(of the system \(see Fig. 7, p. 217\). Further, the sectional area of) Tj T*
(the two collecting ducts will be less than that of one main duct, and) Tj T*
(greater uniformity of flow thereby secured. Where the two ducts join) Tj T*
(up into the single duct of the fan, the bends must be easy; otherwise) Tj T*
(the draughts would collide and neutralize one another. Branch ducts,) Tj T*
(if they cannot be made tangential to a rounded curve, should enter) Tj T*
(the main duct at an angle of 30 degrees, as by so doing equalization) Tj T*
(of the draught at different openings is made fairly uniform. The very) Tj T*
(common defect of a right-angle joint diminishes the draught by nearly) Tj T*
(one-half. Branch ducts should never be made to enter a main duct on the) Tj T*
(outer side of a bend, because at this point the pressure of the current) Tj T*
(of air inside the duct is increased. They should join up on the inside) Tj T*
(of a bend, where the pressure is reduced.) Tj T*
