(CHAPTER XIII) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(PREVENTIVE MEASURES AGAINST LEAD POISONING--_Continued_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=Periodical Examination.=--In various codes of regulations a surgeon) Tj T*
(is required to make periodical medical examination of the workers.) Tj T*
(The term ?surgeon? is defined as the ?Certifying Factory Surgeon of) Tj T*
(the district, or a duly qualified medical practitioner, appointed) Tj T*
(by written certificate of the Chief Inspector of Factories, which) Tj T*
(appointment shall be subject to such conditions as may be specified) Tj T*
(in that certificate.? The wording of the regulation varies somewhat) Tj T*
(in different codes, but the intention in all is the same, and the) Tj T*
(following example from the Tinning Regulations will indicate the) Tj T*
(purpose and scope:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  ?Every person employed in tinning shall be examined by the surgeon) Tj T*
(  once in every three months \(or at such shorter or longer intervals as) Tj T*
(  may be prescribed in writing by the Chief Inspector of Factories\),) Tj T*
(  on a day of which due notice shall be given to all concerned. The) Tj T*
(  surgeon shall have the power of suspension as regards all persons) Tj T*
(  employed in tinning, and no such person after suspension shall be) Tj T*
(  employed in tinning without written sanction from the surgeon entered) Tj T*
(  in the health register.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  ?Every person employed in tinning shall present himself at the) Tj T*
(  appointed time for examination by the surgeon. No person employed) Tj T*
(  in tinning shall, after suspension, work at tinning without written) Tj T*
(  sanction from the surgeon entered in the health register.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Under the Special Rules for white-lead works, examination is required) Tj T*
(at weekly intervals; under the Special Rules for Earthenware and) Tj T*
(China, Manufacture of Litho-Transfers and Red Lead, and under the) Tj T*
(Regulations for Electric Accumulators, and Paints and Colours, monthly;) Tj T*
(under the Regulations for Tinning, Yarn dyed with Chromate of Lead,) Tj T*
(and Enamelling, at quarterly intervals, subject to the limitation or) Tj T*
(extension specified in the regulation quoted.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The limitation as to quarterly examination is useful to meet) Tj T*
(conditions, on the one hand, where special incidence calls for) Tj T*
(increased safeguards; and, on the other, relaxation, by reason of) Tj T*
(adoption of special processes or measures lessening risk. Thus, in) Tj T*
(a yarn-dyeing factory, in consequence of occurrence of six cases) Tj T*
(within five months, a weekly instead of a quarterly examination was) Tj T*
(prescribed. After eight months, as no further cases were reported, a) Tj T*
(monthly examination was substituted for the weekly, and eventually,) Tj T*
(with continued absence of illness, the normal quarterly examination was) Tj T*
(resumed.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
