(the manner suggested, be necessary, he will recognize that transference) Tj T*
(to a non-lead process, if feasible, is preferable to entire cessation) Tj T*
(from work in very many cases. The surgeon, therefore, should know what) Tj T*
(departments are possible alternatives to lead work.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The fact that an examination is made on factory premises, is directed) Tj T*
(to detection and prevention, treatment taking a subordinate place, and) Tj T*
(is often made on persons who, unlike hospital patients, seek to conceal) Tj T*
(their symptoms, causes it to be an examination _sui generis_. Hence) Tj T*
(the surgeon must trust his sight more than his hearing. A surgeon with) Tj T*
(experience of such work has said: ?The worker in lead must be surveyed) Tj T*
(as an individual, and idiosyncrasies must be carefully studied and) Tj T*
(allowed for; the ?personal equation? is of vital importance?[1].) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For the examination a well-lighted room affording privacy is essential.) Tj T*
(While it is desirable for the surgeon periodically to see the processes) Tj T*
(and conditions under which work is carried on, systematic examinations) Tj T*
(of workers should not be made elsewhere than in a private room. The) Tj T*
(custom of marshalling workers in a queue, although perhaps unavoidable) Tj T*
(in many cases, is liable to detract from the seriousness of the) Tj T*
(proceedings, a sense of which it should be one of the aims of the) Tj T*
(examination to arouse. In discussing the method of interrogation and) Tj T*
(usual examination, Dr. King Alcock[2], Certifying Factory Surgeon of) Tj T*
(Burslem, says: ?Note the general manner assumed in answering questions) Tj T*
(and any indications of carelessness in dress and toilet. Inquire) Tj T*
(into the state of digestion, existence of colicky pains, regularity) Tj T*
(of bowels, menses, history of pregnancies and miscarriages, whether) Tj T*
(before, in the intervals of, or during lead employment; existence of) Tj T*
(headache, diplopia, or amaurosis. Note the type, facies, state of teeth) Tj T*
(and nails, complexion, speech, tongue, strength of grasp \(if possible,) Tj T*
(with dynamometer\), any tremor in outstretched hand, resistance to) Tj T*
(forcible flexion of wrist.... If strabismus is present, note whether of) Tj T*
(old standing or recent; and if ocular troubles seem imminent, examine) Tj T*
(for optic neuritis, either at once or at home \(this is very important,) Tj T*
(as cases of acute and serious optic neuritis still baffle examination) Tj T*
(by their intermensual development\).? He recommends the surgeon, apart) Tj T*
(from entry in the health register, which must necessarily be very) Tj T*
(brief, to keep a private notebook, and to enter in it as a matter of) Tj T*
(routine such details as name, process, age, duration of employment,) Tj T*
(condition \(married or single\), pregnancies, state of bowels and menses,) Tj T*
(dental toilet, and any special point worthy of note in individual) Tj T*
(workers. A card index, if in use, might conveniently serve for such) Tj T*
(entries.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In the actual routine examination it may be useful to describe the) Tj T*
(procedure where a large number of workers pass before the surgeon in a) Tj T*
(white-lead works every week. The points noted are:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. The general appearance of the man as he walks forward, especially) Tj T*
(the face with regard to anæmia, which in the majority of cases of early) Tj T*
(lead absorption is not a true anæmia, but is due to vaso-motor spasm) Tj T*
(of the arterioles of the face and eyes. Frequently, on speaking to a) Tj T*
