() Tj T*
(In some factories all new workers are examined by the surgeon before) Tj T*
(they commence work in dangerous processes. At any rate, a list of such) Tj T*
(persons should be given to the surgeon at his visit, as naturally) Tj T*
(the question of personal fitness for employment should be decided) Tj T*
(at his first examination. Conditions which should lead to rejection) Tj T*
(are tubercular disease of every kind, idiopathic epilepsy, all forms) Tj T*
(of mental disease or weakness \(hysteria, feeble-mindedness, and) Tj T*
(neurasthenia\), obvious alcoholism, women who are pregnant or who give) Tj T*
(a history of repeated miscarriages prior to work in lead, persons with) Tj T*
(marked errors of refraction unless corrected by glasses, kidney disease) Tj T*
(of all kinds, evidence of previous chronic saturnism, and bad oral) Tj T*
(sepsis. Special attention will have to be paid to casual labourers, and) Tj T*
(it should be the aim of the surgeon to discourage this class of labour) Tj T*
(in lead industries. Work under special rules or regulations requires) Tj T*
(to be carried out under strict discipline, and this it is extremely) Tj T*
(difficult to maintain on other than regular workers, who recognize the) Tj T*
(need for cleanliness and observance of regulations.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Other aids to diagnosis cannot be carried out as a matter of) Tj T*
(routine, but will necessarily be used in particular cases, such as) Tj T*
(ophthalmoscopic examination of the fundus, electrical reactions of) Tj T*
(muscles, analysis of the urine, and examination of the blood-pressure.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A few words may be added on the significance of the two commonest) Tj T*
(signs--the blue line and anæmia. It cannot be too strongly insisted) Tj T*
(on that presence of the Burtonian line on the gums is, as a rule,) Tj T*
(indicative of lead absorption, and not of lead poisoning. As a) Tj T*
(danger signal its value is immense, and hardly less so its value in) Tj T*
(clinching diagnosis in doubtful cases. Whenever the line is seen risk) Tj T*
(is imminent, and poisoning \(not necessarily of the individual in whom) Tj T*
(it is pronounced\) among the workers is inevitable in the absence of) Tj T*
(adoption of precautions. Unfortunately, careful dental toilet, which) Tj T*
(the surgeon will necessarily lay stress on, may prevent development,) Tj T*
(or the practice, when adopted, cause disappearance of the line after) Tj T*
(the lapse of a few months. Under these circumstances, the merest trace) Tj T*
(will have all the significance of the fully-developed line in a worker) Tj T*
(neglectful of care of the teeth. Among new workers a commencing blue) Tj T*
(line should be strong evidence of the need for dust removal at some) Tj T*
(point in the process of manufacture. The line, in our experience, is) Tj T*
(dense in occupations giving rise to fumes or to dust of compounds of) Tj T*
(lead, but comparatively rare in those handling metallic lead or its) Tj T*
(alloys, as compositors, tea-lead rollers, solderers, and the like.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
