(Sometimes a rule is made that no lead-worker who has suffered from an) Tj T*
(attack of plumbism should be allowed to resume work. This we consider) Tj T*
(too harsh a measure. It may be true for painters, but when remedial) Tj T*
(measures, such as locally applied exhaust ventilation, can be applied,) Tj T*
(with consequent removal of the danger in the process at which the) Tj T*
(poisoning has arisen, prohibition of employment seems an unnecessarily) Tj T*
(drastic measure.) Tj T*
