(CHAPTER XIV) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(PREVENTIVE MEASURES AGAINST LEAD POISONING--_Continued_) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=Overalls and Head Coverings.=--Stress has been laid on the wearing) Tj T*
(of overalls and head coverings in processes giving rise to dust or to) Tj T*
(splashes of glaze or paint in special rules and regulations in the) Tj T*
(past. With the improvement that has taken place in exhaust ventilation,) Tj T*
(they have become less important. Indeed, the aim of all manufacturers) Tj T*
(and ventilating engineers should be to render processes so free of dust) Tj T*
(as to make them altogether unnecessary. Increasing knowledge of the) Tj T*
(insidious manner in which lead dust can arise has shown that from this) Tj T*
(point of view overalls of the cotton or linen material ordinarily worn) Tj T*
(constitute a real source of danger. Splashes of glaze dry on them, and) Tj T*
(at every movement involving rubbing of the surface dust is generated.) Tj T*
(Some operations almost oblige the worker to press the article worked) Tj T*
(upon against the chest, so that chance of inhalation of dust from) Tj T*
(this source alone is considerable. Taking them off creates dust, and) Tj T*
(after this is done a reprehensible practice exists of either shaking) Tj T*
(or beating them against a post. In large factories they are usually) Tj T*
(washed on the premises, and the water in which this is done will become) Tj T*
(a solution containing some lead in suspension. Hence, even when washed) Tj T*
(and dried ready for wear, overalls may not be quite free of lead. Apart) Tj T*
(from the general obligation recognized that an employer should provide) Tj T*
(and maintain everything necessary to guard against danger contracted) Tj T*
(in his factory, we think that the risk run by a worker in taking the) Tj T*
(overall home and washing it there is negligible, and offers advantages) Tj T*
(in the ultimate cleanliness of the overall over washing on factory) Tj T*
(premises. Laundresses shaking overalls prior to washing them have been) Tj T*
(known to contract plumbism.) Tj T*
ET
