(=Meal-Room Accommodation.=--Wherever lead processes are carried on the) Tj T*
(provision of a mess-room is called for in a part of the factory remote) Tj T*
(from possible contamination from lead dust. This we hold on general) Tj T*
(grounds of cleanliness and self-respect, and not because we think the) Tj T*
(eating of meals in rooms where lead is used would noticeably increase) Tj T*
(the number of cases. The more conveniently situated in relation to the) Tj T*
(workrooms the mess-room is, the more will it be used. Set out briefly,) Tj T*
(the requirements of a mess-room are that it should be--) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Well ventilated, warmed, and lighted.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Not less than 10 feet high, and with floor-space ample for each) Tj T*
(person likely to occupy it at any one time.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Have walls the surface of which is smooth and impervious to a height) Tj T*
(of at least 4 feet from the ground.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Have pigeon-holes or other arrangement in which each person can) Tj T*
(deposit his food separate from that of others.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Have means of warming and cooking food.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. Be kept properly clean and dry.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(No part of a factory becomes so unsightly in the absence of daily) Tj T*
(cleaning as a mess-room, especially where provision has only to be made) Tj T*
(for five or six workers.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
