() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=Floors.=--These should be smooth and impervious. Wood flooring can) Tj T*
(hardly be regarded as coming within this category; it is unsuitable) Tj T*
(where lead processes are carried on. Preference must be given to floors) Tj T*
(of concrete and the like material, which can be washed down easily) Tj T*
(rather than swept. Frequently the dust raised in sweeping the floor) Tj T*
(has determined an attack of lead poisoning. No objection can be raised) Tj T*
(to wooden grids and iron roll matting placed on the concrete floor for) Tj T*
(the workers to stand on. Cold feet and transference of lead dust by the) Tj T*
(boots are lessened by their use. Where traffic is heavy, as is often) Tj T*
(the case in lead works, vibration is set up with wooden floors, and) Tj T*
(dust disseminated. In smelting works cast-iron plates are serviceable) Tj T*
(as flooring.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=Instruction of the Worker.=--Too much stress cannot be laid on this) Tj T*
(point. To insist upon it, however, is useless unless the occupier has) Tj T*
(installed the necessary exhaust ventilation, and equipped his factory) Tj T*
(with the other essentials for enabling the workman to guard against) Tj T*
(dust and free his hands of adhering lead, in whatever form. When this) Tj T*
(has been done, then the worker himself can do something.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Often he creates dust unnecessarily. In shovelling out of a cask with) Tj T*
(spade or trowel, in order to get out the last trace of the material to) Tj T*
(be transferred, he generally gives it a knock, which causes dust to) Tj T*
(fly so sharply as to escape the exhaust; or he removes the implement) Tj T*
(quickly from the exhaust, before it has been completely emptied and) Tj T*
(while dust is still being given off. He will use a brush to clean his) Tj T*
(bench in preference to cleaning it by a wet method. The printer may) Tj T*
(hold type between his teeth. Many workers bite their nails. Moustache) Tj T*
(and beard may be fingered, and because of this workers may even be) Tj T*
(advised to be clean-shaven. They may chew or smoke constantly while at) Tj T*
(work, and will frequently eat with unwashed hands.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Notices enjoining care and cleanliness may be, and often are, hung) Tj T*
