() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=Lead Smelting and Silver Refining.=--Lead poisoning very rarely occurs) Tj T*
(in lead mining in Europe, as galena \(sulphide of lead\), the principal) Tj T*
(ore in which the metal is found, is insoluble. Galena always, and other) Tj T*
(lead ores very often, contain a small proportion of silver, ranging) Tj T*
(from 0·001 to 1 per cent., and at times traces of gold. Owing to the) Tj T*
(great affinity of lead for silver, lead smelting is necessarily a) Tj T*
(process preliminary to the extraction of silver and gold from it[1].) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Lead ores, drosses, etc., on arrival at the factory, are, after) Tj T*
(sampling, deposited in bins or heaps \(often in the open air\), and) Tj T*
(watered to prevent dust. All ores may, and refractory ores \(containing) Tj T*
(over 4 per cent. silica\) and dross must, be smelted in a blast furnace) Tj T*
(by aid of coke. The bulk of the charge in a blast furnace may consist) Tj T*
(of more or less complex ores of the precious metals, especially silver.) Tj T*
