(=Spelter \(Zinc\) Manufacture.=--Lead is present in zinc ores in a) Tj T*
(proportion of from 1 to 10 per cent. \(usually 3 per cent.\). Despite) Tj T*
(this small proportion, incidence of chronic plumbism among those) Tj T*
(engaged in the manufacture is high, as in the present state of) Tj T*
(knowledge the lead fume given off in distillation of the zinc cannot) Tj T*
(be efficiently removed. Blende \(zinc sulphide\) is first calcined, and) Tj T*
(the residue, after mixture with calamine \(zinc ashes\) and anthracite,) Tj T*
(forms the charge for the furnace. The retorts are arranged in long) Tj T*
(rows one above the other, and frequently back to back in the furnace,) Tj T*
(so that there may be 250 or more to each furnace, and of the furnaces) Tj T*
(there may be several in a shed. Attached to the retort is a fireclay) Tj T*
(receptacle \(condenser\) into which the zinc distils, and an iron nozzle) Tj T*
(\(prolong\) to prevent oxidation in the condenser. While distillation) Tj T*
