(=Manufacture of Red and Orange Lead and Litharge.=--These processes) Tj T*
(are frequently carried on as part of lead-smelting works. Red lead is) Tj T*
(produced by oxidation, first, of metallic pig-lead, in a reverberatory) Tj T*
(furnace at dull red heat, into massicot \(yellow monoxide\). During the) Tj T*
(process the material is constantly raked. The massicot is withdrawn) Tj T*
(from the furnace, and subsequently, after drying and sieving, is again) Tj T*
(subjected to similar treatment at slightly lower temperature. Orange) Tj T*
(lead is made by treating white lead in the manner described.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
