(manufacture of red lead was 108, of which 47 were attributed to work at) Tj T*
(the furnaces, 43 to packing and sieving, and 16 occurred among general) Tj T*
(labourers, part of whose duty it was to sweep up the floors. Collis) Tj T*
(estimates the attack rate in the five years 1905-1909, in a certain) Tj T*
(number of factories employing 171 persons, at 50 per 1,000. Reference) Tj T*
(to the table on p. 48 shows that the proportion of those suffering from) Tj T*
(encephalopathy is higher than in any other industry--an observation) Tj T*
(previously noted by Layet[9].) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
