(containing dilute acetic acid. Ten to fifteen of such layers \(blue) Tj T*
(beds\) one on the top of the other are built into the stacks to a height) Tj T*
(of some 20 feet. When completed, the stacks remain for 80 to 100 days) Tj T*
(before being emptied. During this period the temperature rises to 75°) Tj T*
(to 80° C., considerable evolution of carbonic acid gas takes place, and) Tj T*
(the lead is converted first into acetate and subsequently the white) Tj T*
(basic carbonate. The layers \(white beds\) are uncovered and the corroded) Tj T*
(strips \(corrosions\) collected by hand. They are placed in trays and) Tj T*
(carried to heavy steel rollers by means of which and subsequent raking) Tj T*
(in wash becks the carbonate is detached from the uncorroded central) Tj T*
