(During subsequent wet processes of grinding danger is mainly from) Tj T*
(splashing. From the settling tanks the white lead is pumped into) Tj T*
(filter presses, and the resulting cake is dried. Here the considerable) Tj T*
(risk from splashing is again almost unavoidable. Concrete floors are) Tj T*
(necessary. Emptying the stoves involves much handling, with inevitable) Tj T*
(creation of dust, especially when the bowls are withdrawn from the) Tj T*
(racks. Risk has been greatly lessened by reducing the height of) Tj T*
(the shelves to 10 feet and prohibiting the piling of one bowl upon) Tj T*
(another. Mechanical drying stoves into which men need not enter either) Tj T*
(for filling or drawing are now commonly met with. Of these there) Tj T*
(are various types--\(1\) Horses similar to those common in laundries,) Tj T*
(which can be withdrawn on rails; \(2\) small chambers built up one upon) Tj T*
(another somewhat in the form of gas retorts in a gasworks, heated by) Tj T*
(steam jackets and coils, each chamber containing only two or three) Tj T*
(cakes of white lead pulp, the cakes themselves being removed by a) Tj T*
(mechanical process from the press into the drying chambers; \(3\) bogies) Tj T*
(carrying the white lead in bowls on racks made to pass through the) Tj T*
(tunnel-like stove; \(4\) drying machines--_i.e._, closed cylinders fitted) Tj T*
(with a series of platforms so arranged that they may be charged with) Tj T*
(white lead on one side, and so fixed as to be turned round by means) Tj T*
(of mechanical appliances. When dry, the material is discharged into) Tj T*
(a chute by a series of scrapers into a small enclosed compartment,) Tj T*
(holding the barrel to be filled. With the drying machine, however,) Tj T*
(there is considerable risk of dust leakage, especially when the doors) Tj T*
(are opened. In packing by hand, safety depends on efficient exhaust) Tj T*
(ventilation when the contents are tipped into the barrel, but a danger) Tj T*
(constantly present is that, to get through the work quickly, the bowls) Tj T*
(may be withdrawn from the influence of the exhaust before the last) Tj T*
(traces of dust have been removed from the bowl. Mechanical packing, by) Tj T*
(means of a large bladed screw forcing the white lead into the barrel,) Tj T*
(which as it becomes filled is lowered automatically, is everywhere) Tj T*
(desirable. An essential condition of this method is that a dust-proof) Tj T*
(collar should connect the automatic packer with the barrel. Some dust) Tj T*
(almost inevitably escapes, and a hood and exhaust should be provided,) Tj T*
(however perfectly the machine is said to act.) Tj T*
