() Tj T*
(1. _Glaze Processes._--The charge of glaze is made by weighing) Tj T*
(out and mixing carbonate of lead with the necessary silicates and) Tj T*
(silico-borates in the lead house or mixing-room, where wet grinding) Tj T*
(prepares the mixture for the dipping-tub. ?Putters-up? hand the ware) Tj T*
(to the dipper, from whom ?takers-off? place it on boards for removal) Tj T*
(to the drying still, or place it \(in large works\) directly on to the) Tj T*
(shelf of an appliance known as a ?mangle,? in which an endless chain) Tj T*
(carries the ware through a heated chamber. Subsequently superfluous) Tj T*
