(other parts of the articles. This ware cleaning is performed with a wet) Tj T*
(sponge or flannel, either while the ware is still moist or by scraping,) Tj T*
(the particles removed dropping into a vessel of water; or, if the glaze) Tj T*
(is dry, over a grating provided with exhaust draught. The ware is next) Tj T*
(removed by the glost-placer on boards, and each piece is separately) Tj T*
(placed by him in the sagger \(fireclay receptacle\) and carried into an) Tj T*
(oven to be fired.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. _Decorative Processes._--Majolica painting is the application of a) Tj T*
(coloured glaze rich in lead by means of a brush. Ground-laying consists) Tj T*
