(To reduce risk or remove the danger of lead poisoning in this industry,) Tj T*
(use of low solubility glazes or of leadless glazes are advocated. On) Tj T*
(this point the Lead Committee say: ?The effect of melting the lead) Tj T*
(with silicious matter amounts to imprisoning it in such a manner as) Tj T*
(to render it less liable to the action of the acids which it meets in) Tj T*
(passing through the human body, and in consequence largely reduces the) Tj T*
(likelihood of its absorption into the blood. If the frit is properly) Tj T*
(compounded, all but a small fraction of the lead is rendered insoluble,) Tj T*
(and glazes so made are spoken of as ?low solubility glazes.? The) Tj T*
(finished glaze generally contains from 12 to 22 per cent., or more, of) Tj T*
(lead oxide, but after the process of fritting with sufficient silicious) Tj T*
(material only from 2 to 5 per cent. remains soluble.?[A]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(  [A] Raw lead comprises red lead, white lead, and litharge. If) Tj T*
(  introduced in this form as a constituent of glaze it is soluble in) Tj T*
(  dilute acids. If, however, the raw lead is fluxed by heating with a) Tj T*
(  part or the whole of the silica, it is converted into ?fritted lead.?) Tj T*
(  The solubility of the frit depends upon the relative proportions of) Tj T*
(  material taken. Thorpe[23], as a result of numerous analyses of lead) Tj T*
(  silicates \(after determining their solubility as regards lead\), both) Tj T*
(  simple and complex, in use in the potteries and on the Continent,) Tj T*
(  found that the quantity of lead dissolved had no necessary relation) Tj T*
(  to the quantity of lead in the silicate. ?Primarily and in the main) Tj T*
(  the insolubility of the lead depends not upon any one oxide or group) Tj T*
(  of oxides, but upon the maintenance of a certain proportion between) Tj T*
(  the whole of the basic oxides on the one hand and the whole of the) Tj T*
(  acidic oxides on the other. If the value of ratio bases/acids is) Tj T*
(  higher than, or approximately equal to, two, the amount of the lead) Tj T*
(  extracted is small, but if it fall much below two, the quantity of) Tj T*
(  lead dissolved begins rapidly to increase.?) Tj T*
