(analyzed in the Government Laboratory was found to contain 26·66 per) Tj T*
(cent. of lead oxide. The fact that all the lead used is in the form of) Tj T*
(a silicate, even although the silicate is readily soluble in dilute) Tj T*
(acid, tends, we believe, to cause incidence of poisoning to be less) Tj T*
(than might have been expected from the amount of dust often present in) Tj T*
(the air, and attacks, when they occur, to be less severe, as a rule,) Tj T*
(than they would be were raw carbonate of lead alone used. For the) Tj T*
