() Tj T*
(=Manufacture of Electric Accumulators[30].=--Electric accumulators) Tj T*
(are secondary batteries which serve for the storage of electricity,) Tj T*
(in order to allow of a current when desired. A primary battery is) Tj T*
(one in which the materials become exhausted by chemical action, and,) Tj T*
(unless a portion or the whole of the materials is renewed, fails to) Tj T*
(supply electricity. The secondary battery becomes exhausted in the) Tj T*
(same way, but the chemical contents are of such a nature that it is) Tj T*
(merely necessary to pass a current of electricity through the battery) Tj T*
(\(charging\) in order to recharge them. In the accumulator battery the) Tj T*
(positive element is peroxide of lead, and the negative element spongy) Tj T*
(lead. The elements--several positive connected together and several) Tj T*
(negative--are placed in dilute sulphuric acid contained in vessels of) Tj T*
(glass.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The form of accumulator in almost universal use now is the pasted) Tj T*
(plate, but it varies greatly in size, according to the use for which) Tj T*
(it is required. It may be either large, to act as an equalizer or) Tj T*
(reservoir of current in electric-lighting installations, or quite small) Tj T*
(for ignition purposes in motor-cars. The litharge smeared on to one) Tj T*
(plate becomes converted into the positive element, peroxide of lead,) Tj T*
(during what is called the ?forming process? \(passage of the electric) Tj T*
(current through the dilute sulphuric acid solution in which it is) Tj T*
(placed\), and red lead smeared on to the other becomes spongy lead to) Tj T*
(form the negative.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The industry gives employment to about 1,200 persons. Plates are first) Tj T*
(cast in moulds from a bath containing molten lead or of lead with) Tj T*
(admixture of antimony. Irregularities in the plates so cast are removed) Tj T*
(by a saw or knife \(trimming\), and sometimes filed or brushed with a) Tj T*
(wire brush. The interstices in the plates are next filled in by means) Tj T*
(of a spatula with paste of litharge or red lead, as the case may be,) Tj T*
(which has been previously mixed either by hand at the bench or in a) Tj T*
(special mechanical mixing machine. After drying, the plates are removed) Tj T*
(to the formation room to be charged. To allow of the passage of the) Tj T*
(current, positive elements are connected together, and negative also,) Tj T*
(by means of a soldering iron or, more frequently, of an oxy-hydrogen) Tj T*
(blowpipe flame. After formation is complete the plates have to be) Tj T*
(built into batteries, or ?assembled.? Tailpieces, technically known as) Tj T*
(?lugs,? have to be connected with each plate, effected usually by the) Tj T*
