(In a small factory the cask of white lead is broken and the material) Tj T*
(scooped out into a pail. Scales are at hand, and when the amount of) Tj T*
(lead removed weighs half a hundredweight the contents of the pail are) Tj T*
(discharged either into a cylindrical pug-mill or into the pan of an) Tj T*
(edge-runner to be mixed with oil. In large factories the dry white lead) Tj T*
(is generally shovelled directly from the cask down openings or shoots) Tj T*
(in the floor to the grinding mills below.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
