(all kinds of painting with use of white lead. Finally, in 1909, a law,) Tj T*
(to take effect from 1914, was passed prohibiting the use of white lead) Tj T*
(in paint altogether.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In Belgium, following on regulations issued under royal decree in 1905,) Tj T*
(in which, among other things, quarterly periodical medical examination) Tj T*
(of house-painters was required, the law dated August 20, 1909, came) Tj T*
(into force, prohibiting the sale, transport, and use, of white lead in) Tj T*
(the form of powder, lumps, or small pieces, and requiring, if intended) Tj T*
(for the purpose of painting, the white lead to be mixed ready ground in) Tj T*
(oil. Dry-rubbing and sandpapering are also prohibited.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
