(regulations dated June 27, 1905, of which the following are the main) Tj T*
(provisions: \(1\) Prohibition of actual contact with white lead in) Tj T*
(grinding and mixing, and adequate protection from the dust so created;) Tj T*
(\(2\) mechanical incorporation of the white lead with the oil or varnish,) Tj T*
(and prevention of the escape of dust into the workroom; \(3\) preliminary) Tj T*
(moistening prior to scraping, chipping off, or rubbing down, dry oil) Tj T*
(colours; \(4\) and \(5\) provision of overalls and washing accommodation,) Tj T*
(including soap, nailbrushes, and towels \(in erection of new buildings) Tj T*
(the workmen must be able to wash in a place free from frost\); \(7\)) Tj T*
(instruction of the workman by the employer as to the risk attaching) Tj T*
(to the work by supplying him with a copy of the regulations and) Tj T*
(cautionary notice. Further, where painting operations are carried on) Tj T*
(in factories or workshops as subsidiary to other processes, there must) Tj T*
