(and Austrian factories.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Periodical medical examination at quarterly intervals has been) Tj T*
(instituted in the principal factory, with good results, as it enables) Tj T*
(those who show early signs of lead absorption to be transferred to) Tj T*
(other processes. Exhaust ventilation has been tried, but, except at the) Tj T*
(few lathes where cleaning alone is done, without complete success, in) Tj T*
(view of the nature of the work.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=Shot-making.=--Cases in shot-making arise from the dust given off when) Tj T*
(sifting the shot into different sizes--an operation which should be) Tj T*
(carried on in sieves entirely closed in and under negative pressure.) Tj T*
(Dust collected from the glass casing over a sifting machine contained) Tj T*
(60·3 per cent. of metallic lead. The sample was free from arsenic.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=Heading of Yarn dyed with Chromate of Lead.=--Cotton yarn is dyed \(10\)) Tj T*
(on a considerable scale with chromate of lead, chiefly for Oriental) Tj T*
(markets; and it is the orange chrome--that most heavily weighted with) Tj T*
(lead--which is most in demand there. The orange chrome colour is) Tj T*
(obtained by dipping hanks of yarn into solution of lime, and then into) Tj T*
(acetate of lead. The process is repeated a second time, after which) Tj T*
(the chromate is formed by dipping in bichromate of soda, and finally) Tj T*
(boiling in lime-water[39].) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In production of yellow chrome colour, the yarn is treated only once) Tj T*
(in a bath of lead acetate. Other colours made are lemon chrome and \(by) Tj T*
(addition of an indigo bath\) chrome green.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The early processes of dyeing rarely give rise to poisoning, but the) Tj T*
(strong solution of bichromate of soda readily causes characteristic) Tj T*
(ulceration of the skin--?chrome holes.? Danger arises from dust in) Tj T*
(the process of heading or ?noddling,? as it is sometimes called, of) Tj T*
(the dried yarn over posts. The hanks of yarn are tugged and shaken by) Tj T*
(women as a rule, and in the case of orange chrome very considerable) Tj T*
(quantities of dust are liberated. We have been told that a hank of this) Tj T*
(kind of yarn does not commend itself to an Oriental buyer unless, when) Tj T*
(shaken, dust is visible.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The industry was certified as dangerous in 1895, in view of serious) Tj T*
(illness and death in Glasgow and Manchester, and special rules were) Tj T*
(made to apply, not only to the heading operations, but also to the) Tj T*
(winding, reeling, and weaving, of the dyed yarn--processes in which) Tj T*
(cases of poisoning are very rare.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Detailed inquiry was made in 1906 in eleven factories where yarn was) Tj T*
(dyed on a considerable scale by means of chromate of lead--in eight) Tj T*
(mainly for export to India, and in three for the home market. Yarn dyed) Tj T*
(for the home market gives off less dust when headed, as the material) Tj T*
(undergoes additional washing in water and in dilute acid; and it is) Tj T*
(also sometimes passed through a sizing of starch, which fixes the) Tj T*
