(\(1\) The draught here was obtained from the main chimney-shaft. The) Tj T*
(small velocities at the end post, it was subsequently found, arose from) Tj T*
(the fact that the double heading post was connected by means of a very) Tj T*
(small duct to the end of the large duct which served the other posts.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(2\) Wooden duct connected up with fan. The area of the openings into) Tj T*
(the duct could be enlarged or diminished by means of a shutter. The) Tj T*
(figures in brackets were those obtained when the shutter was fully) Tj T*
(opened.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(3\) In this factory originally a 2 foot 6 inch fan was simply placed) Tj T*
(in the wall. Subsequently they were boxed in and ducts of wood brought) Tj T*
(within a foot of the noddling bar. Four of the branch ducts were found) Tj T*
(to be blocked.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(5\) Wooden ducts and hoods behind bar both close to the fan.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(6\) Circular metal ducts with curved angles, and placed about 8 to 10) Tj T*
(inches behind post; all connected up with a 4 foot 6 inch fan. The) Tj T*
(small velocities \(120 feet\) at two posts was due to loose connection of) Tj T*
(the branch ducts allowing air to be drawn in at the foot.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(7\) Metal duct distant about 2¹?? feet from the post, and situated) Tj T*
(immediately below and not behind the bar. Dust was prevented from) Tj T*
(rising above the post by a glass screen, the projection of which also) Tj T*
(prevented the worker from coming too near to, or getting his head over,) Tj T*
(the post.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(8\) Metal ducts, 9¹?? inches in diameter. Evidence of ill-health was) Tj T*
(greatest here, notwithstanding good draught, because the branch ducts) Tj T*
(were not brought close enough to the point where ?heading? was done,) Tj T*
(but were distant 15 inches from the centre of the post, and ?noddling?) Tj T*
(was done at a distance of 2 feet from the duct, one man standing) Tj T*
(between the draught and the bar.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(10\) Draught arranged as in \(7\), below the bar, without protection of) Tj T*
(the worker by a glass screen.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Regulations now apply to the industry. So clear is it that) Tj T*
(locally-applied exhaust ventilation is of paramount importance in) Tj T*
(prevention of poisoning, that, however intermittent the operation) Tj T*
(of ?heading,? exemption from this requirement cannot be permitted.) Tj T*
(Determination periodically by the occupier of the speed of the draught) Tj T*
(at each exhaust opening should prevent blockage of ducts.) Tj T*
