() Tj T*
(The regulations do not apply to the winding of, and weaving with,) Tj T*
(yarn dyed with chromate of lead. Rarely in the spinning and weaving) Tj T*
(factories of Blackburn does the amount of the particular yarn in) Tj T*
(question constitute as much as 5 per cent. of the total quantity of) Tj T*
(_coloured_ yarn used. Section 74, 1901, is sufficient to meet the) Tj T*
(isolated cases where injury to health arises. The habit of biting) Tj T*
(chrome-dyed thread has given rise to lead poisoning. Nor do the) Tj T*
(regulations apply to treatment of calico or cloth into which lead may) Tj T*
(enter. Such poisoning as may occur must be practically confined to) Tj T*
(persons employed in the paint-mixing house.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(=Manufacture of India-rubber.=[9]--Litharge, massicot, red lead, and) Tj T*
(sulphide of lead, are generally mixed with rubber. Litharge is regarded) Tj T*
(not only as a valuable filler for rubber, but has the faculty of) Tj T*
(hastening vulcanization. All dry-heat goods depend upon it where a dark) Tj T*
(or black effect is wanted.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Every year a few cases are reported in the process of mixing the) Tj T*
(batches in the weighing room of the rubber factory, or more frequently) Tj T*
(at the hot calender rolls, where the batch of dry powder containing) Tj T*
(the lead compound is gradually distributed by hand on to the rubber) Tj T*
(so as to effect an intimate mixture. The heated air over the rollers) Tj T*
(causes dust to rise. According to the purpose for which the rubber is) Tj T*
(wanted, the quantity of litharge in the batch varies. In one factory of) Tj T*
(fourteen men employed at the calender rolls, ten showed a blue line,) Tj T*
(five were markedly anæmic, one had weakness of the wrists, and two) Tj T*
(weakness of grasp[40]. Only one case has been reported since exhaust) Tj T*
(ventilation was applied locally over each calender roll. In a rubber) Tj T*
(tyre factory five cases followed one another in quick succession,) Tj T*
(all in persons employed on the rolls. There should be no hesitation) Tj T*
(in requiring exhaust ventilation wherever employment in mixing the) Tj T*
(batches or at the rolls is constant. In general, however, the work in) Tj T*
(weighing out is intermittent, and reliance is placed on the wearing of) Tj T*
(a respirator.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(No attempt has been made to enumerate all the industries and processes) Tj T*
(in which lead poisoning may arise. The task would become wearisome, as) Tj T*
(they are so numerous. Nor is it necessary to give details of all that) Tj T*
(are known, as it is doubtful whether there can be any different in) Tj T*
(nature or requiring different treatment from the many which have been) Tj T*
(described.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
